  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Let $(v,w)$ be the solution of the following system. What is the value of $v+w?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.5v-2.5w=7.5 \\\\ 0.7v+0.3w=2.9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "To get rid of the decimals, we multiply both equations by $10,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.5v-2.5w=7.5 & |\\times 10 \\\\ 0.7v+0.3w=2.9 & |\\times 10\\end{aligned}\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}5v-25w=75 \\\\ 7v+3w=29\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can solve for $v$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5v-25w & =75 \\\\ 5v & =25w+75 \\\\ v & =\\frac{25w+75}{5} \\\\ v & =5w+15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the value of $w,$ we can substitute $v=5w+15$ into the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7v+3w & =29 \\\\ 7(5w+15)+3w & =29 \\\\ 35w+105+3w & =29 \\\\ 38w & =-76 \\\\ w & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $w=-2$ into the equation $v=5w+15$ to get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =5w+15 \\\\ v & =5(-2)+15 \\\\ v & =-10+15 \\\\ v & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $v=5,\\,w=-2.$ So,\n\n$$\nv+w=5+(-2)=3.\n$$",
